  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rights and leadership training for indigenous and campesino communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pastoral Social Caritas Bolivia run a national rights and leadership training programme. The programme aims to strengthen the rural campesino and indigenous organisations to enable them to assert their rights and influence public policies, especially when communities are affected by extractive and mega-project activity. Caritas Bolivia work to do this by teaching  the local communities about their rights and the issues they face and training them in advocacy techniques and then support them to run campaigns based on the needs and interests of the communities involved. 
NB: Caritas Bolivia were formerly known until 2014 as CEPAS or CEPAS Caritas</narrative>
  </description>
